# Creating a token puts it onto the battlefield (CR 111.1, 701.7a), so Land Equilibrium replaces the creation of a land token
# by an opponent with as many lands as its controller (1 to 1): Bot2's Relm's Sketching makes a token copy of Bot1's
# Island, which enters under Bot2's control, and then Bot2 sacrifices a land of their choice - the token itself, which is on
# the battlefield by then (CR 614.6). A token in the graveyard ceases to exist (CR 111.7).
[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Land Equilibrium
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Relm's Sketching
Black Lotus
Forest
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Land Equilibrium.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Relm's Sketching.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Island)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Types = Land
Bot2.Choose(Island)
[T4 Bot2.End]
[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Types = Land
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Types = Land
